<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio de Berrío</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1527–1597</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio de Berrío was a Spanish conquistador and governor who devoted his last years to the search for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-dorado">El Dorado</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco">Orinoco</a>. In 1592 he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-jose-de-oruna">San José de Oruña</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> as a base for his expeditions. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-raleigh">Walter Raleigh</a> burned the town and captured him in 1595.</p></div>
